      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -7, 15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 14, -11 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To compute $\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na - 3b &= ⟨ - 7, 15⟩ - 3 \\cdot ⟨14,-11⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 7, 15⟩ - ⟨42,-33⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 7 - 42, 15 - (-33)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 49, 48⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
